["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>You will hear quail and read their sign far more often than you see them. Tracks, dust bowls, droppings and calls tell you a covey lives here and roughly when it was here.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a dirt lane beside a brush edge. Shallow round dusting bowls in the dirt, small three toed tracks, and a grey body feather. Washington Fish and Wildlife says dusting holes, tracks and droppings show quail are near, 75 percent. Tip: dusting happens at midday, so check the spot then.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusting bowls on a dirt lane</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#e6d3b0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">brush edge</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"210\" cy=\"130\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"280\" cy=\"165\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M240 200 l-4 -8 M244 200 l0 -9 M248 200 l4 -8 M262 214 l-4 -8 M266 214 l0 -9 M270 214 l4 -8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M330 120 q10 -8 16 2 q-8 4 -16 -2 Z\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/>\n<text x=\"338\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">feather</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bowls</text>\n<text x=\"254\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tracks</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"236\" width=\"380\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusting holes, tracks, droppings: birds near (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday dusting spot: come back at noon (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Look for tracks, droppings and dusting holes near cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Then walk the road edge in short bursts <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the sign method in full</summary><ul><li>Washington Fish and Wildlife: \"drive or hike back roads, looking for tracks, droppings and dusting holes that indicate there may be birds nearby.\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>\"When you find evidence of birds, walk the edge of the road in short bursts, stopping often near patches of roadside cover.\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>Do it legally: no shooting across or within the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Road allowance\">Road allowance</button>, and stay off private land without permission (99%, Rule Book).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bird tracks drawn on a grid of 1 centimetre squares. A quail track, about 3.5 centimetres long, a Tip from a related quail, VERIFY. A grouse track, about 5 centimetres, 75 percent. Both show three toes forward and a short hind toe. Quail walk with prints in one line, one in front of the next, 60 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tracks on a 1 cm grid</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"40\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"60\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"120\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"140\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"160\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"180\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"200\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"220\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"240\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"260\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"280\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"300\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"320\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"340\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"360\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"380\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"44\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"84\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"144\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"144\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"164\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"184\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"#e2dccd\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M110 180 L110 110\"/><path d=\"M110 180 L78.5 124.0\"/><path d=\"M110 180 L141.5 124.0\"/><path d=\"M110 180 L110 192.6\"/></g>\n<g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M280 194 L280 94\"/><path d=\"M280 194 L235.0 114.0\"/><path d=\"M280 194 L325.0 114.0\"/><path d=\"M280 194 L280 212.0\"/></g>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail: about 3.5 cm</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip, VERIFY)</text>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grouse: about 5 cm</text>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(75%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Prints in one line, one ahead of the next (60%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Three toes forward, a short hind toe; prints in one line (60 to 75%).</li><li>Quail track about 3.5 cm long (Tip, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tracks in full</summary><ul><li>Quail forage on the ground, so tracks usually fall in a single line, one foot in front of the other (60%, Bear Tracker).</li><li>Sandy river bars and dusty lanes show quail tracks best <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Size: a related quail (Gambel's) track measured about 3.8 by 3.8 cm (1.5 in) (60%, Wildwood Tracking quiz). For California quail, a working figure of about 3.5 cm: Tip, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with a ruler on a fresh print.</li><li>Grouse tracks are about 5 cm (75%, the app's habitat tour). Chukar and pheasant tracks are bigger than quail: measure and write it down (Tip).</li><li>The hind toe often does not show; in fine dust it can <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Tracking basics: <a href=\"#/s/tracks\">Tracks</a> and <a href=\"#/s/sign\">Reading sign</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels. One bird dropping: a dark coil with a white cap of urates, 70 percent. A roost pile: many droppings under a roost tree, because California quail roost in dense trees or shrubs, 70 percent. Chukar roost on the ground under rock ledges and sagebrush, so piles collect there, 80 percent. Tip: a fresh pile means the covey roosts there now.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Droppings and roost piles</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"40\" width=\"182\" height=\"180\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"206\" y=\"40\" width=\"182\" height=\"180\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<path d=\"M70 120 q30 -26 50 0 q-18 20 -50 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b5a3a\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"114\" cy=\"112\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"103\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One dropping</text>\n<text x=\"103\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dark coil,</text>\n<text x=\"103\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">white cap (urates)</text>\n<text x=\"103\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(70%)</text>\n<path d=\"M260 160 l20 -70 l20 70 Z\" fill=\"#556b2f\"/>\n<rect x=\"276\" y=\"150\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<g fill=\"#6b5a3a\"><ellipse cx=\"270\" cy=\"182\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"282\" cy=\"186\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"294\" cy=\"182\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"288\" cy=\"190\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"276\" cy=\"191\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"297\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost pile</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">under a</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">roost tree</text>\n<text x=\"297\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">quail: trees (70%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"230\" width=\"380\" height=\"62\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar: piles under rock ledges and sage (80%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fresh pile = covey roosts here now (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bird droppings: a dark coil with a white cap <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A pile under a roost tree marks a covey's bedroom (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: droppings in full</summary><ul><li>Birds pass nitrogen waste as uric acid, the white part of the dropping (70%, Poultry Hub).</li><li>California quail roost in dense trees or shrubs, not on the ground <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>, so look for droppings under thick conifers, junipers or shrub clumps near feeding cover (Tip).</li><li>\"Watch for roost piles... Fresh roost piles often indicate good places to find birds early or late in the day.\" (60%, Missouri Conservationist 1996, written about bobwhites, which roost on the ground)</li><li>Chukar roost on the ground under sage or juniper and among rocks, in coveys, sometimes tail to tail (80%, FEIS): piles collect under ledges.</li><li>Do not handle droppings with bare hands (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a dirt lane beside a brush edge. Shallow round dusting bowls in the dirt, small three toed tracks, and a grey body feather. Washington Fish and Wildlife says dusting holes, tracks and droppings show quail are near, 75 percent. Tip: dusting happens at midday, so check the spot then.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusting bowls on a dirt lane</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#e6d3b0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">brush edge</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"210\" cy=\"130\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"280\" cy=\"165\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M240 200 l-4 -8 M244 200 l0 -9 M248 200 l4 -8 M262 214 l-4 -8 M266 214 l0 -9 M270 214 l4 -8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M330 120 q10 -8 16 2 q-8 4 -16 -2 Z\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/>\n<text x=\"338\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">feather</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bowls</text>\n<text x=\"254\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tracks</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"236\" width=\"380\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusting holes, tracks, droppings: birds near (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday dusting spot: come back at noon (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Quail dust bathe as a group, often at midday (70 to 75%).</li><li>Round bowls in loose soil with small tracks around them (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: dusting in full</summary><ul><li>Dust bathing is a daily communal habit of quail (60%, Wikipedia summary). Washington Fish and Wildlife names dusting as a favourite midday pastime, often at road edges <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>One summary says the bowls are about 7 to 15 cm across: Tip, the figure is unsourced (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Tip: fresh bowls have loose, fluffy dust and a feather or two. Old bowls crust over and catch leaves.</li><li>Chukar use dusting sites at midday too <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-pair.jpg\" alt=\"Body feathers are grey and brown; plume feathers are black.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Body feathers are grey and brown; plume feathers are black. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: BLM Nevada, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California_Quail_Fallon_NV_(19978763835).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A small pile of feathers can mean a hawk kill (Tip).</li><li>Single grey body feathers at a dust bowl: birds were here (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: feathers in full</summary><ul><li>Predators of quail include Cooper's and sharp shinned hawks and great horned owls <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. A plucked pile on open ground often marks a hawk kill (Tip).</li><li>A pile of feathers is sign of a covey's range, not of where the covey sits now (Tip).</li><li>Shot birds: find every feather patch where a bird fell and search from there (Tip). See chapter 10.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table of California quail calls. Assembly call, chi CA go or cu CA cow, loudest on the middle note: given by a bird separated from the covey or as the covey moves. Contact calls, soft clucks and pips, while feeding. Alarm, sharp pit pit, when danger is close. Advertising call, one loud cow, by unpaired males in spring. Fighting call, squill, by males sorting rank in spring. 70 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail calls and what they mean</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Call</text>\n<text x=\"185\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sounds like</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">When</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Assembly</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"60\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;chi CA go&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lost, or covey moving</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"104\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Contact</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"104\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">soft clucks, pips</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feeding together</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"148\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#a33b2a\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Alarm</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"148\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sharp &quot;pit pit&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Danger close</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"192\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Advertising</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"192\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">one loud &quot;cow&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring, unpaired male</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"236\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fighting</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"236\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;squill&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring, males sort rank</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">From bird guides (70%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Dawn and dusk calling tells you where a covey roosts <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Point to the sound, note the cover, hunt it next morning (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: calls in full</summary><ul><li>Assembly calls start the covey's move off the roost at first light <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A chorus of calls at dusk as birds gather to roost (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>Hunters can start the chorus with a quail call and use the answers to find spots for the next morning <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. A mouth call is legal; recorded or electronic calls are not for game birds (99% for the electronic ban, 95% for mouth calls, Rule Book).</li><li>Soft clucks while feeding: you hear them only when you are quiet and close <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table of fresh versus old sign, a Tip. Droppings: fresh are moist, dark and shiny; old are dry, pale and crumbly. Tracks: fresh have sharp edges; old are blurred or pocked by rain. Dust bowls: fresh have loose dust; old are crusted with leaves in them. Feathers: fresh are clean and fluffy; old are flat and dirty. Note the last rain or wind: it dates the sign.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How fresh is it? (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"130\" y=\"40\" width=\"126\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"193\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fresh</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"40\" width=\"126\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#9a9ca2\"/>\n<text x=\"325\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Old</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Droppings</text>\n<rect x=\"130\" y=\"78\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"193\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">moist, dark, shiny</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"78\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"325\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dry, pale, crumbly</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Tracks</text>\n<rect x=\"130\" y=\"124\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"193\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sharp edges</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"124\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"325\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rain pocked, blurred</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Dust bowl</text>\n<rect x=\"130\" y=\"170\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"193\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">loose fresh dust</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"170\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"325\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">crusted, leaves in it</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Feathers</text>\n<rect x=\"130\" y=\"216\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"193\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">clean, fluffy</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"216\" width=\"126\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"325\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">flat, dirty</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Note the last rain or wind: it dates the sign</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Moist and dark: today. Dry and pale: days old (Tip).</li><li>Note the last rain or wind; it dates every sign (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: freshness in full</summary><ul><li>No study gives aging times for quail sign. All of this is Tip.</li><li>Tracks after rain: crisp prints on a rain pocked surface were made after the rain stopped (Tip).</li><li>Morning dew: a dark line where birds walked through dewy grass is from this morning (Tip).</li><li>Write sign in the Journal with the date and the weather. After a season, you know each covey's routine (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Follow a covey, step by step</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 1 of following a covey: at first light or dusk, stand still on a road edge and listen for the chi CA go assembly call. Point toward the sound and note the cover.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 1 Listen</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(70 190)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<path d=\"M90 180 q40 -40 80 0 M100 170 q30 -30 60 0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"36\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;chi CA go&quot;</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 160) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dawn or dusk: stand still, listen</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Dawn or dusk: stand still and listen for calls.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 2: walk the road edge toward the calls and read the sign: tracks, droppings and dusting bowls show where the covey feeds and loafs.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 2 Read the sign</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"170\" width=\"380\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#e6d3b0\"/>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M120 200 L120 178\"/><path d=\"M120 200 L110.1 182.4\"/><path d=\"M120 200 L129.9 182.4\"/><path d=\"M120 200 L120 203.96\"/></g>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M160 196 L160 174\"/><path d=\"M160 196 L150.1 178.4\"/><path d=\"M160 196 L169.9 178.4\"/><path d=\"M160 196 L160 199.96\"/></g>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M200 200 L200 178\"/><path d=\"M200 200 L190.1 182.4\"/><path d=\"M200 200 L209.9 182.4\"/><path d=\"M200 200 L200 203.96\"/></g>\n<ellipse cx=\"270\" cy=\"190\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"110\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"34\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tracks</text>\n<text x=\"270\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dust bowl</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tracks and dust bowls point to cover</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Walk toward them reading tracks and dust bowls.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 3: walk the edge of that cover slowly, stopping every few steps, so hiding birds lose their nerve and flush. Stop for 15 to 20 seconds, Washington Fish and Wildlife, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 3 Stop and go</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"120\" rx=\"150\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(80 200)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(160 200)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stop 15 to 20 s</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk, stop 15 to 20 s, walk (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Walk the cover edge: stop 15 to 20 seconds often.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 4: after the flush, watch each bird down and mark where singles land. Walk straight to the nearest single first. Singles often hold tight, Washington Fish and Wildlife, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 4 Mark the singles</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"120\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"250\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(60 200)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"240,98 234.2,106.1 230.0,98.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"310,170 301.5,175.3 300.6,166.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"186\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"104,128 103.2,138.0 95.7,133.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark every single. Go to the nearest.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> After the flush, mark every single.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Listen, read, stop and go, mark (Tip and 75%).</li><li>Two hunters: one on each side of the cover (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: following in full</summary><ul><li>Stop at each patch of cover and wait at least 15 or 20 seconds before moving on; hiding quail may get nervous and fly (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>Move quickly from patch to patch, but stop at each one <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Mark the singles and go to the nearest first. Singles often hold tight <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Move slowly and quietly so you can hear a distant covey rise or see birds flying in (60%, Missouri Conservationist).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 4: after the flush, watch each bird down and mark where singles land. Walk straight to the nearest single first. Singles often hold tight, Washington Fish and Wildlife, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 4 Mark the singles</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"120\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"250\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(60 200)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"240,98 234.2,106.1 230.0,98.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"310,170 301.5,175.3 300.6,166.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"186\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"104,128 103.2,138.0 95.7,133.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark every single. Go to the nearest.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Tracks in a line, dust in a bowl, white capped drops: the covey's on patrol.\" (Tip)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"15 to 20\": stop 15 to 20 seconds at each patch <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Sign order:</strong> ears, lanes, bowls, brush. Listen, check the lane, find the bowls, walk the brush (Tip).</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"A fresh dust bowl at noon means birds within a stone's throw.\" Widely repeated hunter lore (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Washington Fish and Wildlife, Bear Tracker, Wildwood Tracking, FEIS, Poultry Hub, Missouri Conservationist, the app Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68963\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington Fish and Wildlife: quail hunting</a> and <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68922\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chukar hunting</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://bear-tracker.com/quail.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bear Tracker: California valley quail</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wildwoodtracking.com/quiz/quiz042/quiz042A.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildwood Tracking quiz 42 (Gambel's quail track)</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/database/feis/animals/bird/alch/all.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">US Forest Service FEIS: chukar</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.poultryhub.org/anatomy-and-physiology/body-systems/circulatory-system\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Poultry Hub Australia: circulatory system (uric acid)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://mdc.mo.gov/node/245855\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Missouri Conservationist: Quail hunting without dogs (Smith 1996)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 (60%, bobwhite).</li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikipedia: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11, dust bathing only (60%; bowl size unsourced).</li><li><a href=\"https://ncrcd.specialdistrict.org/files/b900df31f/California-Quail-info.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California Wildlife Habitat Relationships: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: predators <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book: legal methods, calls and decoys</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-where-you-can-hunt\">where you can hunt</a>, 2 October 2026 edition (95 to 99%).</li></ul></details>"]